request.description:
Issues a single-use UUID with a 2-minute TTL.

The nonce is stored in Redis (or in-memory Map) and atomically deleted on first use.

✅ EXPECTED: Status 200 with { nonce, expiresAt }

⚠️ GPS is sent via WebSocket in queue:join, not via HTTP.

For this scene:
1. In the WebSocket, emit queue:join with Sao Paulo GPS:
```json
{
  "mode": "RECREATIONAL_2V2",
  "betAmount": 0,
  "gps": { "lat": -23.5505, "lng": -46.6333, "accuracy": 15 }
}
```
2. Wait 15 seconds
3. Emit again with Manaus GPS:
```json
{
  "mode": "RECREATIONAL_2V2",
  "betAmount": 0,
  "gps": { "lat": -3.1190, "lng": -60.0217, "accuracy": 15 }
}
```

This /auth/me request just confirms the token is working.
